Old iMessage notifications can reopen their conversation.

This commit's message describes a README fonts section. It ALSO carries an
unrelated change to BarWidget.qml and ui.test.ts, swept in by a catch-all
`git commit` from a concurrent session while that work was still uncommitted
in the shared working tree. This note exists so the notification work is
findable, since the subject line will never match a search for it.

WHAT: Blip toasts now carry Omarchy's `omarchy-exec-argv` hint, a persisted
      argv of ["qs","-p","/usr/share/omarchy/shell","ipc","call",
      "nixfred.blip","goto","<chat>"].
WHY:  --action=default lives inside the notify-send process and dies with the
      toast after 8s, so a row in the notification center was inert. The hint
      is persisted by the notification service, so an old row still opens the
      conversation days later.
HOW:  Leading "+" stripped (qs ipc call reads it as a flag; show() matches the
      bare digits as an alias); chat id shape-checked and passed as its own
      argv element, never inside a shell string.

